    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d565-a1">

                <pb facs="0782" n="676" sameAs="frus:frus1906p1/pg676"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of Commerce and Labor to Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of Commerce and Labor,<lb/>Office of the
                                Secretary</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1906-02-09"><hi rendition="#italic">February 9,
                        1906</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: At the request of the commissioner of
                    fisheries, I have the honor to transmit herewith, for the confidential
                    information of the Department of State, extracts from two personal letters
                    regarding the Newfoundland fisheries question received by Mr. A. B. Alexander,
                    who represented this department on the Newfoundland coast during the past
                    season.</p>
                <p>A copy of the commissioner’s letter is also transmitted herewith for your further
                    information in the matter.</p>
                <p>Respectfully,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">V. H. Metcalf</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
